	(text "5V buck (U101): switching regulator, VIN (9-30 V) to the board's +5V rail"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 15.24 12.7 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2.54 2.54)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "2faba4bf-d211-5d7b-a1f9-249b7275cca7")
	)
	(text_box "WHAT IT DOES\nU101 (LM2596) is a step-down switching regulator. It switches the protected vehicle supply VIN_LM on and off at 150 kHz;\nL101 and C104 smooth the pulses into 5.29 V DC (+5V_PSU). D101 joins it onto the board's +5V rail, which USB can also feed\n(through D201 in the ESP32 + USB module). +5V feeds the 3.3 V regulator, CAN, DOUT1, the GPS port and the +5 V sensor output.\n\nPINS OF THIS MODULE (its block on the top sheet)\nVIN_LM (in): protected vehicle supply from the VIN input module (after D103)\n+5V (out): the board's 5 V rail, about 4.9 V after D101\nGND: ground\nPower and ground reach the parts on this sheet only through these pins: the ground and supply symbols drawn on this sheet are local to it."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 15.24 17.78 0)
		(size 265 24.5)
		(margins 1.5 1.5 1.5 1.5)
		(stroke
			(width 0.1524)
			(type solid)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "7bdf4e37-28b5-57d1-b987-0cccd922b08a")
	)
	(rectangle
		(start 81.28 104.14)
		(end 167.64 129.54)
		(stroke
			(width 0.1524)
			(type dash)
			(color 200 60 0 1)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(uuid "24d7481a-ed3f-5a99-b3e0-b84f4a2fbcec")
	)
	(text "HOT LOOP: keep this tiny on the PCB"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 81.88 104.74 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.0 1.0)
				(color 200 60 0 1)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "6d4922dc-6a86-5c98-aed9-73f8c49164b4")
	)
	(text "Hot loop: C103 and C102 right at U101 pin 1 (VIN), D105 right at pin 2 (OUT), and the GND pads of\nC102, C103, D105 and U101's tab (pin 3) joined by short, wide copper with vias into the GND plane.\nLM_SW (pin 2 - D105 - L101) is the noisiest copper on the board: short and 1.4-1.5 mm wide, far from\nAIN1 and the magnetometer U602 (20 mm or more). R103/R104 next to pin 4; keep LM_FB away from L101.\nOn this board D105 is about 14 mm from pin 2: U101's pins face C102 while D105 and L101 sit on the far\nside of its tab (the same compromise as the routed board, see its README). A tight loop needs U101, D105,\nL101 and C102 rearranged so the pins face D105 and L101."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 81.28 134.62 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
				(color 200 60 0 1)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "52471cad-5987-5ef7-af8a-7118d62f9f14")
	)
	(text_box "PARTS AND THEIR JOBS\nU101: LM2596S-ADJ 3 A step-down regulator (TO-263). Pin 5 (ON/OFF) to GND = always on. It adjusts its switching so FB (pin 4) sits at 1.23 V.\nC102: 220 uF 50 V input bulk capacitor: supplies U101's pulsed input current.\nC103: 100 nF 50 V input high-frequency capacitor: the one closest to U101 pin 1.\nD105: SS54 Schottky catch diode: carries the inductor current while U101's switch is off.\nL101: 33 uH 3 A inductor: stores energy each switching cycle; with C104 it turns the pulses into DC.\nC104, C105: 220 uF 16 V output bulk capacitor and 100 nF high-frequency capacitor: low ripple on +5V_PSU.\nR103, R104: Feedback divider 3.3k / 1k: +5V_PSU = 1.23 V x (1 + 3.3k / 1k) = 5.29 V.\nD101: SS34 Schottky OR-ing diode onto +5V: this stage and USB (through D201) can both feed +5V without pushing current into each other.\nR105, D106: 2.2k + red LED: lights while the 5V buck runs (about 1.5 mA)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 15.24 156 0)
		(size 155 24.5)
		(margins 1.5 1.5 1.5 1.5)
